<!-- MSVC /Od shapes: each function stores its argument registers into the
     Windows x64 home slots at entry RSP+8..+0x20. caller spills ecx, edx,
     r8d and r9b and reloads only the r9b slot, to pass it fifth of nine
     arguments to callee; unused2 spills two and reads neither; mixed spills
     edx and xmm0 and reads edx; negatives stores rbx, r8 into rcx's slot and
     a zeroed r9; reused spills rdx and then keeps a local in that slot.
     Bytes from homespill_pe_x86_64.py. vararg and spillhigh are variadic
     int f(const char *fmt, ...) shapes (llvm-mc -triple=x86_64): vararg is
     MSVC /Od's, which spills all four registers and takes the address of
     rdx's slot for va_start (mov [rsp+0x20],r9; mov [rsp+0x18],r8;
     mov [rsp+0x10],rdx; mov [rsp+0x8],rcx; sub rsp,0x18; lea rax,[rsp+0x28];
     mov [rsp],rax; mov rax,[rsp+0x20]; movsx eax,byte [rax]; add rsp,0x18;
     ret), and spillhigh is gcc -O2's, which saves rdx, r8 and r9 without
     a va_start (movsx eax,byte [rcx]; mov [rsp+0x10],rdx;
     mov [rsp+0x18],r8; mov [rsp+0x20],r9; ret). -->
